        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Owney\n- Places: Albany, New York; New York City; Hudson River; Mohawk River\n- Organizations: Albany post office\n- Roles: postal mascot\n- Topics: geography\n\nFacts:\n- Owney was born around 1887 and died on June 11, 1897.\n- Owney was a stray Border terrier.\n- About 1888, the Albany post office adopted Owney as its first unofficial postal mascot.\n- Albany, New York, is roughly 150 miles north of New York City.\n- Albany developed on the west bank of the Hudson River.\n- Albany is about 10 miles south of the confluence of the Hudson River and the Mohawk River.",
